## Why This Is Asked

Assesses offline-first design, delta-based syncing, and conflict handling under intermittent connectivity, which are critical in collaboration apps used by teams.

## Key Concepts

- Core Data data model for Comment and Patch objects
- Delta/patch format including baseVersion, changes, and timestamps
- Reconciliation strategy (latest-writer-wins or server-validated merges)
- Robust test plan for offline edits, re-connect, and concurrency

## Code Example

```javascript
// Swift-like pseudocode: apply a patch to a Comment
func apply(patch: Patch, to comment: inout Comment) {
    // Validate base version matches current state
    guard patch.baseVersion == comment.version else {
        // Handle conflict resolution
        resolveConflict(patch: patch, comment: &comment)
        return
    }

    // Apply delta changes
    for change in patch.changes {
        switch change.type {
        case .insert:
            comment.text.insert(change.text, at: change.position)
        case .delete:
            comment.text.removeSubrange(change.range)
        case .replace:
            comment.text.replaceSubrange(change.range, with: change.text)
        }
    }

    // Update version and timestamps
    comment.version += 1
    comment.updatedAt = Date()
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests advanced offline-first architecture, CRDT-based conflict resolution, and iOS persistence strategies that scale across devices operating in disconnected environments.

## Key Concepts
- **CRDT OR-Set**: Enables automatic merging of concurrent offline edits without requiring central coordination
- **Append-only event log**: Provides crash-safe durability and enables idempotent replay on startup
- **Multi-modal data modeling**: Survey (container), Response (user input), Media (file references with metadata)
- **Deterministic conflict resolution**: Timestamp-based last-write-wins with user-facing conflict flags for manual resolution when needed
- **Durable persistence**: Realm or SQLite for structured data, with file-backed storage for media
- **Crash-safe resume**: Replay log on launch to reconstruct state and resume interrupted operations

